ess></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>JAPAN SCIENCE AND TECHNOLOGY CORPORATION</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SAKANAKA, MASAHIRO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SATO, KOHJI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TANAKA, JUNYA</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SAKANAKA MASAHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SATO KOHJI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TANAKA JUNYA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SAKANAKA, MASAHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SATO, KOHJI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TANAKA, JUNYA</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>Preparations for efficaciously administering ginsenoside Rb1 or its salt useful as cell-protective agents. More particularly, medicinal compositions for inhibiting apoptosis or apoptosis-like cell death or medicinal compositions for promoting the expression of a cell death inhibitory gene product Bcl-xL which contain ginsenoside Rb1 or its salt; and preparations for intravenous administration which contain ginsenoside Rb1 or its salt. The above medicinal compositions contain ginsenoside Rb1 or its salt at a low concentration, preferably 1 ng/ml or less and still preferably 1 to 100 fg/ml. These compositions have effects of promoting the expression of the cell death inhibitory gene product Bcl-xL and inhibiting apoptosis or apoptosis-like cell death. The above preparations for intravenous administration are useful in treating or preventing, in particular, brain and nervous diseases.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne des préparations permettant une administration efficace de ginsenoside Rb1 ou de son sel, utiles comme agents protecteurs de cellules. Plus particulièrement, l'invention concerne des compositions médicinales inhibant l'apoptose ou la mort cellulaire du type apoptose, ou des compositions médicinales activant l'expression d'un produit de gène inhibant la mort cellulaire, Bcl-xL, qui contient du ginsenoside Rb1 ou son sel ; et des préparations s'administrant par voie intraveineuse qui contiennent du ginsenoside Rb1 ou son sel. Les compositions médicinales en question contiennent du ginsenoside Rb1 ou son sel à une faible concentration, de préférence égale ou inférieure à 1 ng/ml, et se situant idéalement entre 1 et 100 fg/ml. Ces compositions ont pour effets d'activer l'expression du produit de gène inhibant la mort cellulaire, Bcl-xL, et d'inhiber l'apoptose ou la mort cellulaire du type apoptose. Les préparations en question s'administrant par voie intraveineuse sont utiles pour traiter ou prévenir en particulier des affections cérébrales et nerveuses.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>